{% comment %}
  The colors a storefront surface offers for a product (hide-sold-out-colors):
  every color with an available variant in any size, plus the color the
  surface is currently on, which stays even when sold out (deep links, filter-
  narrowed cards, saved wishlist entries). Output: `|Black|Matt White|`.
  Callers test `offered contains '|' + value + '|'`; the bounding pipes keep
  `Black` from matching `Matt Black`.

  Outputs nothing when the product has no available variant: then every color
  stays, there is nothing to steer the shopper toward.

  Not Dawn's value.available: for a color it depends on the selected size, so
  a color in stock only in another size would read sold out.

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} Product Liquid object
  - color_index: {Number} The color option's zero-based index
  - current: {String} The color the surface is on (optional)

  Usage:
  {% capture offered_colors %}{% render 'ob-offered-colors', product: product, color_index: 0, current: variant.options[0] %}{% endcapture %}
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  if product.available
    assign offered = '|'
    if current != blank
      assign offered = offered | append: current | append: '|'
    endif
    for variant in product.variants
      unless variant.available
        continue
      endunless
      assign token = '|' | append: variant.options[color_index] | append: '|'
      unless offered contains token
        assign offered = offered | append: variant.options[color_index] | append: '|'
      endunless
    endfor
    echo offered
  endif
-%}
